Subject: [PATCH] BaseTools: preserve POSIX quotes in compiler response flags

The GCC path normalization converts escaped string quotes into slashes.
Only normalize Windows paths on Windows. Native POSIX paths already use
forward slashes. Firmware sources and runtime policy are unchanged.
Applies to EDK2 aef4e86045bd151a54d33bab8ae5e8e62462a8f4.

diff --git a/BaseTools/Source/Python/AutoGen/GenMake.py b/BaseTools/Source/Python/AutoGen/GenMake.py
index bbb3c29..db73d97 100755
--- a/BaseTools/Source/Python/AutoGen/GenMake.py
+++ b/BaseTools/Source/Python/AutoGen/GenMake.py
@@ -891,7 +891,7 @@ cleanlib:
                             else:
                                 break
 
-                        if self._AutoGenObject.ToolChainFamily == 'GCC':
+                        if self._AutoGenObject.ToolChainFamily == 'GCC' and os.name == 'nt':
                             RespDict[Key] = Value.replace('\\', '/')
                         else:
                             RespDict[Key] = Value
